Package: folio-cork
Version: 0.5.0
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Installed-Size: 12000
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.35), libgcc-s1, libx11-6, libx11-xcb1, libxcursor1, libxi6, libxcb1, libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libwayland-client0, folio-fonts
Recommends: cups-client, xdg-utils, fonts-dejavu-core, wl-clipboard
Suggests: libreoffice-draw
Maintainer: Ron Shillings <ron.shillings@gmail.com>
Description: diagrams, whiteboards and mood boards
 Folio Cork draws diagrams and runs whiteboards with a ribbon interface,
 KeyTips and ScreenTips: shapes and stencils (flowchart, network, UML,
 database, floor plan, electrical and electronic symbols), connectors that
 stay glued and route around shapes, sticky notes, pen, frames, voting,
 templates, mood boards with colour palettes picked from pictures, comments,
 layers, automatic layout and org charts from a spreadsheet. Opens and saves
 Visio drawings (.vsdx), exports PNG, SVG and PDF, and lets people on the same
 network work on one board together. Everything stays on this computer.
